# Line endings.
#
# .editorconfig mandates end_of_line = crlf for *.cs, but nothing enforced it on checkout, so
# on Linux the files arrived as LF and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` demanded CRLF on
# every line of every file. That is why CI's lint step could never pass.
#
# Store LF in the repository, hand CRLF to the working tree for C# so the formatter and
# .editorconfig agree. Everything else stays LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.cs text eol=crlf

# Verify snapshot files. VerifyChecks.Run enforces these once a .gitattributes exists, and the
# snapshots must stay LF regardless of the C# rule above or every one of them would churn.
*.verified.txt text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.xml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.json text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

# Windows-only tooling that genuinely wants CRLF on disk.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
